<p>Well, I knew it was you the moment I read &quot;Indiana.&quot; <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">You're getting predictable! Downvote.</span></p>
<p>I was with you until the medical examination. Like, the Foundation caught an angry ghost. Okay. The Foundation can un-ghost ghosts. Neat. That's the sort of &quot;spooky supernatural shit that the Foundation takes clinically&quot; that is supercool. It captured what I guess you could call an old-school feel, y'know?</p>
<p>And then a giant blackbox just tore me right the fuck out of it. The ending in general is, for me, a let down. But I enjoyed the rest of it enough, so neutral vote.</p>

